 "notes": "classic: mid-century print rabbit in a flying leap. One closed main contour carries head, body, cotton tail, the near hind foot and the near foreleg; the two ears are back leaves tucked behind the skull, so the head outline itself is the ear root and nothing else shows a seam. Interior lines: haunch crescent, shoulder curve, mouth. Leap: arched back with the hip hump, tail at the back of the rump, single trailing hind foot (the far hind foot sits hidden behind it in leap and shows in gather/stretch), staggered forelegs with flexed paws, lowest ink y 148. Gather: landing crouch, forelegs planted, heels slightly raised; stretch: push-off with feet trailing down-back. The hind foot is a rigid ~105 deg turn between the two (not 180), so the linear in-betweens fold the foot under the haunch instead of collapsing it. Built from anchors (drawing.js) by gen.js; check.js verifies structure, the 8..232 x 8..162 ink box (W 5) and the gather->stretch morph at 21 steps (no winding flip, no self-crossing of the main contour). Small sizes were judged with the page's own heavier strokes (--rw 9-11)."
}